              :plan "On a branch, `(defn ok? ...)` then `(seon.schema/register! :n/thing '[:map [:n/x n/ok?]])` is admitted (the bare symbol resolves as the branch's program predicate). From then on the declared reads of that branch's test step refuse `:malli.core/invalid-schema` naming `n/ok?` from `seon.schema/direct-reference-keys-in` (reached through `seon.db/carried-projection` from `seon.test/definition-digests`), on every later eval request, while reads of the branch head itself answer: a projection built for another value of the branch lacks the branch's predicates. Chain experiment 4 (J1): attempt `ee6cfaeb5c0b` sat 4 min with no end; default's recorded error 7c40461fc9f6 when root's stop read that branch's open turn; reproduced at HEAD 7ef4967db on lane faults-rc's branch (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/db-clean/root-causes.md`). A bare qualified symbol is a Malli reference, and only a projection carrying function contracts resolves it, to the function's contract; the writer's schema-only projection does not. One admission decision: `register!` refuses a function named as a schema (`:seon.schema/function-reference`, `seon.schema/function-references`). The proof's order matters: register! in the eval request that defines the function refuses as an unresolved reference; only a later one admitted it. Done when the test step of such a branch reads it. Read `seon.schema/register!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-4.md`."}
