-             :plan "Owner rule: absence is no key, never nil; no `[:maybe ...]` in a function contract. `seon.merge-test/merge-and-agent-facing-contracts-declare-absence-as-no-key` holds it green for `seon.merge` and every `my.*` namespace; the remaining 460-odd uses in src/ (largest: `seon.turn`, `seon.error`, `seon.db`, `seon.cluster.agent`, `seon.fn`, `seon.render`, `seon.sci.eval`, `seon.render.value`, `seon.error.refusal`, `seon.test.runner`) and resources/seon/schemas (`seon.render.walk`, `seon.print`, `seon.render.value`, `seon.flow`, `seon.source`, `seon.batch`, `seon.render.ns`, `seon.render.var`, `seon.render.test`) convert at their producers one namespace per slice: an optional input becomes an optional map key or another arity, a nil-returning function returns no key or another shape, callers convert in the same commit. Proof to write: widen `maybe-schemas` in that test from the two namespace sets to every first-party namespace as each converts. Read `seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!`, `seon.merge/merge!`, `seon.merge/merge-tx`, `seon.schema/register!`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/context-review/review-3-implement-merge.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/context-review/review-4-cross-task.md`."}
